  "body": "`convertToBlob()` has some confusion in that it queues a task to run something in parallel whereas \"queuing a task\" is all about \"synchronizing\" with the \"main thread\". `toBlob()` goes in parallel only to queue a task.\r\n\r\nPresumably these are both \"asynchronous\" so something can be done in parallel, but it's rather unclear what that is. And also, is it observable, if invoke `toBlob()` followed by a `fillRect()` or some such, can that affect what `toBlob()` returns?\r\n\r\n@whatwg/canvas ",
